Subject: [PATCH] agent: recover peer-bound channel reports and received policy

Layer after monotonic 0191; retain its periodic fallback. A previously completed
ACK cannot recover inventory when a subsequent restart loses both renew and
policy. ACKs prove receipt, not durable controller inventory.

Keep one serialized report per radio. Match MID and reversed Ethernet peers,
invalidate on controller/local-AL changes before retry or ACK, and serialize
report creation with cache updates. Retry identical bytes/MID with monotonic
2/4/8/16/30-second deadlines, at the next existing scheduler opportunity.
Leave BTM ownership and radio protocol state untouched.

Make manager MID dispatch virtual and override only the agent allocator with
an atomic nonzero 16-bit sequence, shared by all agent protocol message types.
The controller allocator implementation is unchanged. Rebuild all agent-side
objects using the updated interface; do not mix old/new class ABIs.

Carry received policy source/destination through the event queue, bind the
retained copy to current peers, and invalidate before deferred WSC replay.
Serialize the existing partial-policy cache and reset its baseline on peer
changes. Retry signed local apply failures without inventing a missing policy.
Renew/policy rearm the publication deadline rather than clearing the sticky
initial-success latch, preserving association refresh while channels are unready.

Extracted regressions cover native allocator concurrency and manager dispatch,
BTM/sibling/stale ACK isolation, peer changes while unready, policy queue/cache
identity, complete native policy byte retention, 100-tick association health,
and real OneWifi translator/encoder disabled flags and emitted field groups.
Existing encoder omissions (traffic separation and vendor client filters) are
not repaired by retaining policy bytes. Candidate admission delays are separate.
This patch is not native-build or live qualified.

Upstream-Status: Pending

